      "id": "GENUS_CINCLUS",
      "name": "Cinclus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Dippers — the only aquatic passerines. These stocky, dark-plumaged birds are perfectly adapted for life along fast-flowing streams. They walk and swim underwater, using their wings to 'fly' against the current while searching for insect larvae among the streambed stones. A transparent third eyelid (nictitating membrane) allows them to see underwater. Their loud, ringing song carries above the roar of rapids.",
      "lineage": "Dippers",
